source: crates/leptoskit_cli/src/cloud/tests.rs
expression: help
---
Primary managed hosting track (LeptosKit Cloud): login, launch, deploy, status, logs, secrets, domains, databases, and usage

Usage: cloud [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  launch        Creates & links a cloud project if needed, previews cost, and ships the first deployment
  deploy        Packs, uploads, and deploys the current project to LeptosKit Cloud
  status        Shows the observed status, hostname, and process readiness of an environment
  logs          Reads recent runtime logs for an environment (pass `--follow` to stream)
  estimate      Previews the resolved release plan and estimated monthly cost without deploying
  open          Opens the environment's live HTTPS URL in your browser
  login         Signs in through your browser with a short code
  logout        Revokes your login and removes the local credentials
  whoami        Shows who is signed in and which organizations they can see
  org           Manages organizations and membership
  project       Manages projects and their production environment
  env           Manages a project's environments
  var           Manages an environment's variables
  secret        Manages an environment's secrets
  domain        Manages an environment's custom domains
  deployments   Lists an environment's deployments, newest first
  rollback      Returns an environment to an earlier deployment that was live, reusing its image
  db            Manages an environment's database and its backups
  publish       Builds the project on a build worker and uploads it to stores, as `lk publish` does, with the environment's secrets as credentials
  publications  Shows an environment's publishes and what they printed
  usage         Shows what the organization used in a month, and its cost
  token         Manages scoped API tokens for CI
  link          Links leptoskit.toml to an existing cloud project
  help          Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
      --url <URL>
          Cloud origin; overrides `LEPTOSKIT_CLOUD_URL` and [cloud].url

      --json
          Prints the documented JSON result

      --org <ORG>
          Organization slug; defaults to [cloud].organization or your personal one

      --project <PROJECT>
          Project slug; defaults to [cloud].project

  -e, --environment <ENVIRONMENT>
          Environment name, for the commands about one; defaults to production

  -h, --help
          Print help

External subcommands:
  Any `leptoskit-cloud-<name>` executable beside `lk` or on PATH (such as `platform`, `worker`, or `control`) can be invoked as `lk cloud <name> [ARGS]...`.
